  "description": "OCOGIA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H98 Dy4 N10 O16,3(C2 H6 O1),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.502-3.880 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.48-112.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(L2)4(NO3)2(μ3-OH)2]·3C2H5OH·8H2O (C90H130Dy4N10O27; H2L2 from 2-hydroxy-5-methylbenzaldehyde and 2,2-dimethylpropane-1,3-diamine). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
